    <item>
      <title>Demystifying the Dark Web Part 1: The Invisible Iceberg</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/operator-blog/posts/dark-web-part1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/operator-blog/posts/dark-web-part1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🛑 [YOUR TURN: Mission Briefing]&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;-your-turn-mission-briefing&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#-your-turn-mission-briefing&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write a 2-3 sentence intro in your &amp;ldquo;Operator&amp;rdquo; voice.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;em&gt;Hint: Mention that as a researcher, understanding these layers is mandatory, not optional.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;The History of the Shadow&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;the-history-of-the-shadow&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#the-history-of-the-shadow&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Most people assume the Dark Web was built by underground cartels. The truth is more clinical: It was built by the &lt;strong&gt;U.S. Naval Research Laboratory (NRL)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Demystifying the Dark Web Part 2: The Onion Handshake</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/operator-blog/posts/dark-web-part-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/operator-blog/posts/dark-web-part-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🛑 [YOUR TURN: The Malware Hook]&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;-your-turn-the-malware-hook&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#-your-turn-the-malware-hook&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write 2-3 sentences here.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;em&gt;As an operator developing the Leviathan loader, why do you care about stealth routing? Mention that hiding a C2 (Command &amp;amp; Control) server is the ultimate defense against a takedown.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Moving Beyond Exit Nodes&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;moving-beyond-exit-nodes&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#moving-beyond-exit-nodes&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Part 1, we talked about how Tor uses three hops to reach the Clearnet. But &lt;strong&gt;Hidden Services (.onion sites)&lt;/strong&gt; are different. They never use an &amp;ldquo;Exit Node.&amp;rdquo; Instead, the circuit stays entirely inside the Tor network.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Demystifying the Dark Web Part 4: The Operator&#39;s Grave</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/operator-blog/posts/dark-web-part-4/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/operator-blog/posts/dark-web-part-4/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🛑 [YOUR TURN: The Cold Open]&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;-your-turn-the-cold-open&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#-your-turn-the-cold-open&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write 2-3 sentences here.&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;Explain that the math of Tor has never been &amp;lsquo;broken&amp;rsquo; in the wild. People aren&amp;rsquo;t caught because the encryption failed; they are caught because they were human. Mention &amp;lsquo;Digital Fingerprints&amp;rsquo;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;The Traffic Correlation Trap&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;the-traffic-correlation-trap&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#the-traffic-correlation-trap&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tor hides your IP, but it cannot hide &lt;strong&gt;Time&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
